{"lean":{"expected":true,"path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GramSignature.lean","via":"ref","ref":"qou:QOU.QBeta.GramSignature.lip_kernel_forces_unbounded","sorry":false,"compiles":"unchecked"},"qa":{"label":"prop:gram-degeneracy-blocks-connes","kind":"proposition","sidecar":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gram-degeneracy-blocks-connes.qa.json","counts":{"pass":56,"bad":0,"na":11,"other":0,"stale":0},"criteria":[{"id":"trap-closing-aphorism","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-em-dash","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-meta-commentary","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-negation-contrast","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"The one rhetorical instance is 'The distance is +infinity as posed, not a hard computation' \u2014 a judgement about difficulty asserted by denial; 'the argument is two lines' would say it positively.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-nonspeakable","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"TWO NUMERICAL ERRORS IN THE FINAL SENTENCE, both verified independently at 40 dps by building the Gram matrix from prop:frobenius-gram-matrix and applying the star (which swaps L+ and L-). The block says: 'At q_0 under convention D the star-form spectrum is 0, 0.752702^{x3}, 4.230339: exactly one null direction, and it is the braid-symmetric one.' (1) MULTIPLICITY: the star form's spectrum is 0, 0.75270211 with multiplicity FOUR, 4.2303392 \u2014 six eigenvalues for a six-dimensional form, signature (5,0,1), which is what prop:frobenius-gram-matrix reports. The quoted x3 lists only five eigenvalues, and x3 is the multiplicity of +0.75270211 in the BILINEAR spectrum (-0.75270211, 0, +0.75270211 x3, +4.23033920). So the bilinear multiplicity has been carried into a star-form sentence \u2014 precisely the confusion prop:frobenius-gram-matrix warns about when it says any statement about the signature must name its pairing. (2) THE NULL DIRECTION IS ANTI-SYMMETRIC, NOT SYMMETRIC. The kernel vector, computed and then normalised, is (1, -0.900918284, -0.900918284, 0.8116537544, 0.8116537544, -0.7312337075) on the NF basis (gamma, sigma_0, sigma_1, L+, L-, e-). Those are exactly (-1/q)^length: -1/q = -0.900918284, 1/q^2 = 0.8116537544, -1/q^3 = -0.7312337075, matching to ten digits. That is the q-ANTIsymmetriser, i.e. the (1^3) alternating block \u2014 which is what rem:frobenius-gram-matrix-context and prop:frobenius-gram-matrix both identify as the radical (y_{(1^3)} = 0 under convention D). The braid-symmetric direction would have coefficients q^length = 1.110, 1.232, 1.368, all positive, and is not in the kernel. Fix: 'exactly one null direction, and it is the braid-antisymmetric one \u2014 the (1^3) block'.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"THE MATHEMATICS OF THE PROPOSITION IS CORRECT: L(a + tk) <= L(a) + |t| L(k) = L(a) keeps the whole line in the unit ball while the objective grows linearly in t, so the supremum is unbounded. The ordered-field scruple in the following paragraph is well taken.","re